: "The ability to participate in conversational repair sequences constitutes an integral part of the language acquisition process (Gallagher, 1977; Garvey, 1975).", "reference": "2002 April 25, Tova Most, “The Use of Repair Strategies by Children With and Without Hearing Impairment”, in Speech & Hearing Services in Schools, volume 33, number 2, →DOI, →ISSN, page 112:"}, {"text": "[...] Salmenlinna and Laakso (2020) studied mother–child conversations using a conversation analysis approach and found that children’s repair requests often occurred in situations where expanding the topic was blocked. Similarly, Yoder et al. (1994) found that repair requests from adults who were attuned to the topic at hand were more likely to trigger repair from children.", "reference": "2024 January 25, Xiaoyan Li, Yonghan Peng, Xinjun Zheng, “The Association Between Mother’s Descriptive Language and Children with Autism’s Conversational Repair: A Moderated Mediation Analysis”, in Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders, volume 54, number 1, →DOI, →ISSN, page 226:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}, {"definition": "The result of repairing something.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["If you look closely you can see the repair in the paintwork."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "изпра́вност"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "riparo"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "korjaus"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "réparation"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Ausbesserung"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Instandsetzung"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "reparo"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "испра́вность"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "reparación"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The condition of something, in respect of need for repair.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["The car was overall in poor repair before the accident. But after the workshop had it for three weeks it was returned in excellent repair. But the other vehicle was beyond repair."], "quotes": [{"text": "The 1300 class (Nos. 1301-16), one of which was damaged beyond repair in an accident, are Co-Cos, weigh 111 tons and have a top speed of 85 m.p.h.", "reference": "1962 March, J. M. Tolson, “The Netherlands Railways today—I”, in Modern Railways, page 172:"}, {"text": "Thirteen houses were damaged beyond repair, and much of the rest of the town suffered broken windows and lost slates.", "reference": "2020 January 12, Benedict le Vay, “The heroes of Soham...”, in RAIL, number 948, page 43:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹɪˈpɛə/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹɪˈpɛɚ/", "tags": ["US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹəˈpɛɚ/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "repairs", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "The act of repairing or resorting to a place.", "tags": [], "examples": ["our annual repair to the mountains"], "quotes": [{"text": "The king sent a proclamation for their repair to their houses.", "reference": "1702–1704, Edward [Hyde, 1st] Earl of Clarendon, (please specify |book=I to XVI), in The History of the Rebellion and Civil Wars in England, Begun in the Year 1641. […], Oxford, Oxfordshire: Printed at the [Sheldonian] Theater:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A place to which one goes frequently or habitually; a haunt.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "There the fierce winds his tender force assail / And beat him downward to his first repair.", "reference": "1667, John Dryden, Annus Mirabilis: The Year of Wonders, 1666. […], London: […] Henry Herringman, […], →OCLC, (please specify the stanza number):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹɪˈpɛə/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹɪˈpɛɚ/", "tags": ["US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɹəˈpɛɚ/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "repairs", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "repairing", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "repaired", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "repaired", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To transfer oneself to another place.", "tags": [], "examples": ["to repair to sanctuary for safety"], "quotes": [{"text": "Go, mount the winds, and to the shades repair.", "reference": "c. 1699 – 1703, Alexander Pope, “The First Book of Statius His Thebais”, in The Works of Mr. Alexander Pope, volume I, London: […] W[illiam] Bowyer, for Bernard Lintot, […], published 1717, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "At the hour of half-past five we repaired to our engagement.", "reference": "1828, [Edward Bulwer-Lytton], chapter XVI, in Pelham; or, The Adventures of a Gentleman. […], volume I, London: Henry Colburn, […], →OCLC, page 111:"}, {"text": "At a late hour, after I had been in bed some time, I heard the visitors repair to their chambers:", "reference": "1847 October 16, Currer Bell [pseudonym; Charlotte Brontë], chapter IV, in Jane Eyre. An Autobiography. […], volume II, London: Smith, Elder, and Co., […], →OCLC, page 109:"}, {"text": "That finished, I repaired to my room, one flight up, and, after a thorough wash, seated myself, pipe in mouth, at the little window that opened on the Rue Garde.", "reference": "1908, W[illiam] B[lair] M[orton] Ferguson, chapter IV, in Zollenstein, New York, N.Y.: D. Appleton & Company, →OCLC, page 47:"}, {"text": "[...] the train engine uncouples and either backs on to the up through line to await its next duty or repairs to the motive power depot.", "reference": "1960 April, B. Perren, “Resorts for Railfans -30: Bournemouth”, in Trains Illustrated, page 239:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "отивам"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "отправям се"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "siirtyä"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "begeben"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["amend", "correct", "fix", "fix up", "furbish", "retrieve", "make whole", "mend", "patch", "put to rights", "rectify", "recondition", "reform", "refurbish", "remediate", "remedy", "renew", "renovate", "restore", "restrive", "revamp", "right"], "antonyms": ["aggravate", "break", "damage", "hurt", "make matters worse"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈriːpɛə/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈriːpɛɚ/", "tags": ["General American"]}], "forms": [{"word": "repairs", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "repairing", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "repaired", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "repaired", "tags": ["past"]}, {"word": "re-pair", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To pair again.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Please try to repair the two earbuds to each other. Place both earbuds back into the charging case, wait for four seconds, then open it and see if they have been repaired with one another."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["amend", "correct", "fix", "fix up", "furbish", "retrieve", "make whole", "mend", "patch", "put to rights", "rectify", "recondi